      "notes": [
        {
          "text": "This indexed schedule (0.65% indexation from 1 May 2026) is replaced by the new Scale of Rates from 10 October 2026, so it is entered as ending on 9 October 2026."
        },
        {
          "text": "The 'Above 75,000 GRT' pilotage row is split across lines in the document; it is read as US$ 45,025.50 + US$ 0.3575 per GRT over 75,000 GRT, which matches the earlier bands.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-indexed-2026-27",
            "page": 11,
            "section": "3.4"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Ships lying at the roadstead for reasons other than waiting for a berth or cargo pay a roadstead charge of US$ 6.15 (coastal Rs. 151.16) per hour or part thereof; waiting for a berth or cargo is free. It is not added to estimates.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-indexed-2026-27",
            "page": 9
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Calls at the single buoy mooring (SBM) have their own tariff (port dues, pilotage with a minimum of US$ 7,325.86, berth hire and tug hire, section 3.5); SBM calls are not priced.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-indexed-2026-27",
            "page": 12,
            "section": "3.5"
          }
        }
      ]
