      "notes": [
        {
          "text": "The new Scale of Rates was notified in the Odisha Gazette (No. 4210) on 10 September 2026 to take effect 'after 30 days from notification'. Paradip Port's own tariff page lists it as 'Scale of Rate w.e.f. 10/10/2026' (paradipport.gov.in, checked 25 October 2026), so it is entered from 10 October 2026."
        },
        {
          "text": "The pilotage minimum (US$ 858 / Rs. 21,110) is stated for the first band; it is applied to the whole charge, which makes no difference above 30,000 GRT.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-2026-new-18092026",
            "page": 18,
            "section": "2.2.1"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Where a ship has two tonnages, the higher one is used for vessel-related charges.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-2026-new-18092026",
            "page": 25
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Ships at berth in the roadstead pay a roadstead charge of US$ 7.38 (coastal Rs. 181.39) per hour or part thereof; ships waiting at the roadstead for cargo operations don't. It is not added to estimates.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-2026-new-18092026",
            "page": 28,
            "section": "2.4"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Calls at the single point or single buoy mooring (SPM/SBM) have their own tariff (port dues, pilotage with a minimum of US$ 8,734.26, berth hire and tug hire, section 2.6); SPM/SBM calls are not priced.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-2026-new-18092026",
            "page": 29,
            "section": "2.6"
          }
        }
      ],
